        height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden" id="tag-manager"></iframe>You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.GroupCreated with Sketch.ProgramsClubsCollege & CareerPathwaysGWC ChallengesCode At HomeGet InvolvedStart a ClubAlumniWays to SupportPartnerCampaignsAbout UsStrategic PlanPublic PolicyResearchOur TeamDonateGet UpdatesWe're on a mission to close the gender gap in tech.AI and EMERGING TECHNOLOGY Breaking down barriers to AI and other emergent technologies.We’ve developed an AI curriculum that will reach over 200,000 students in the U.S; launched two new AI programs and a Data Science course; and are teaching students how to use AI for financial literacy, producing music, and so much more.760,000ServedGirls Who Code has served 760,000 girls, women, and nonbinary individuals330,000AlumniThere are 330,000 Girls Who Code alumni who are college-aged or post-college aged8,000AI StudentsWe taught over 8,000 students about AI through our Summer Programs in 2024 The gender gap in computing is getting worse.In 1995, 37% of computer scientists were women. Today, it’s only 24%. The percent will continue to decline if we do nothing. 

We know that the biggest drop off of girls in computer science is between the ages of 13 and 17.19952017202237%24%22%% of women in Computer Science Girls Who Code is changing the gameWe're reaching girls around the world and are on track to close the gender gap in new entry-level tech jobs by 2030.Support Girls Who Code!Your contribution will help to inspire, educate, and equip girls with the computing skills to become change agents in their communities.Donate Now 14.9BEngagements GloballyThrough our online resources, campaigns, books, and advocacy work - in the U.S. and around the world.760,000Girls, Women and Nonbinary Individuals CodingThrough our in-person programming including our Summer Immersion Program, Clubs, and College Loops50%HUGsOver half of the girls we serve come from historically underrepresented groups. Our ValuesThese are the values that define our organization.BraveryWe believe being brave is about being resilient, persistent, and ambitious.SisterhoodWe believe that diverse ability, culture, identity, and opinion makes our organization stronger.ActivismWe’re not just preparing our girls to enter the workforce - we’re preparing them to lead it, to  improve it, to completely and totally transform it.Girls Who Code is an organization that values diversity, equity, and inclusion as essential to our mission.Read Our Inclusion Statement  Annual Reports202420232022I am a/nAdultStudentBy entering your email address, you are confirming that you are 13+.Sign Up NowContactFAQNewsCareersSign InPrivacy PolicyTerms of UseMedia Kit We use cookies to ensure that we give you the best experience on our website. Learn MoreGot it!window.__APOLLO_STATE__ = {"$ROOT_QUERY.globalSet({\"handle\":\"alertBar\"})":{"name":"Alert Bar","alert":[],"__typename":"alertBar_GlobalSet"},"ROOT_QUERY":{"globalSet({\"handle\":\"alertBar\"})":{"type":"id","generated":true,"id":"$ROOT_QUERY.globalSet({\"handle\":\"alertBar\"})","typename":"alertBar_GlobalSet"},"globalSet({\"handle\":\"co